      "evidence_doc_source_id": "src-win-advanced-audit-policy",
      "availability": "Auditing policy dependent",
      "availability_flags": ["POLICY", "EXPORT"],
      "configuration_required": true,
      "configuration_notes": "Audit categories are enabled by basic or advanced audit policy. Audit Process Creation (events 4688 and 4696) defaults to Not configured; the 'Include command line in process creation events' setting (Administrative Templates\\System\\Audit Process Creation, or Policy CSP ADMX_AuditSettings/IncludeCmdLine) is not enabled by default. Audit Process Termination writes 4689. If basic audit policy overwrites advanced settings, event 4719 is logged; 'Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings' prevents that. Central collection: an Azure Monitor Agent data collection rule with a Windows events data source sends the selected events to the Event table. Custom filters use the form LogName!XPath (XPath 1.0 only); test a filter locally with Get-WinEvent -FilterXPath first. Analytic and Debug channels can't be collected, and event logs must be on a local disk. The Microsoft Sentinel 'Windows Security Events via AMA' connector sends Security and AppLocker events to the SecurityEvent table instead, using the All, Common, Minimal, or Custom event set. In a data collection rule definition, the data source is windowsEventLogs, its filters are in xPathQueries, and the stream is Microsoft-Event.",
